ithub.com/repos/openwizdev/WizSite/issues/comments{/number}","contents_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openwizdev/WizSite/contents/{+path}","compare_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openwizdev/WizSite/compare/{base}...{head}","merges_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openwizdev/WizSite/merges","archive_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openwizdev/WizSite/{archive_format}{/ref}","downloads_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openwizdev/WizSite/downloads","issues_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openwizdev/WizSite/issues{/number}","pulls_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openwizdev/WizSite/pulls{/number}","milestones_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openwizdev/WizSite/milestones{/number}","notifications_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openwizdev/WizSite/notifications{?since,all,participating}","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openwizdev/WizSite/labels{/name}","releases_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openwizdev/WizSite/releases{/id}","deployments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openwizdev/WizSite/deployments","created_at":"2026-11-15T01:10:49Z","updated_at":"2026-11-20T09:38:50Z","pushed_at":"2026-11-24T14:33:09Z","git_url":"git://github.com/openwizdev/WizSite.git","ssh_url":"git@github.com:openwizdev/WizSite.git","clone_url":"https://github.com/openwizdev/WizSite.git","svn_url":"https://github.com/openwizdev/WizSite","homepage":"","size":205874,"stargazers_count":1,"watchers_count":1,"language":"JavaScript","has_issues":true,"has_projects":true,"has_downloads":false,"has_wiki":false,"has_pages":false,"has_discussions":false,"forks_count":0,"mirror_url":null,"archived":false,"disabled":false,"open_issues_count":61,"license":{"key":"apache-2.0","name":"Apache License 2.0","spdx_id":"Apache-2.0","url":"https://api.github.com/licenses/apache-2.0","node_id":"MDc6TGljZW5zZTI="},"allow_forking":true,"is_template":false,"web_commit_signoff_required":false,"has_pull_requests":true,"pull_request_creation_policy":"all","topics":["agent-factory","cloudflare-pages","landing-page","open-source","static-site","website"],"visibility":"public","forks":0,"open_issues":61,"watchers":1,"default_branch":"main","permissions":{"admin":true,"maintain":true,"push":true,"triage":true,"pull":true}},"pull_request":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openwizdev/WizSite/pulls/183","html_url":"https://github.com/openwizdev/WizSite/pull/183","diff_url":"https://github.com/openwizdev/WizSite/pull/183.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/openwizdev/WizSite/pull/183.patch","merged_at":"2026-11-24T13:00:20Z"},"body":"Implements openwizdev/OpenWiz#2966 (BK2: the booking API, spec #2963) on top of BK1 (`lib/book/ical.js`, `slots.js`, `fake.js`) and BK3 (`lib/book/mail.js`, `google.js`) without modifying their files.\n\n## What was built\n\n- **`lib/book/store.js`**:\n  - D1 storage wrapper (`env.BOOK_DB ?? env.ASK_A_WIZ_COUNTERS`) with 5 s timeout on every store call and lazy schema creation (`book_bookings` with partial unique index on `start` where `status = 'booked'`, `book_limits`, and `book_salts`).\n  - Daily-salted SHA-256 IP hashing (`CF-Connecting-IP`, raw IP never stored or logged), constant-time token comparison (`SHA-256` digest XOR), strict 4 KB JSON body reader, and busy-time reader (`fake` -> `fakeBusy`, `live` -> `googleBusy` when `googleReady(env)` else HTTPS-only `BOOK_ICAL_URL` with 10 s timeout, <= 2 MB body cap, and no redirects off HTTPS).\n- **`functions/api/book/slots.js` (`GET`)**: returns `openwiz.book.v1` ascending UTC slots with `Cache-Control: no-store`, 120 req/hr per-visitor limit, `405` on other methods, `503 unavailable` fail-closed on off/misconfigured/DB/calendar failures without leaking secrets.\n- **`functions/api/book/index.js` (`POST /api/book`)** validates same-origin JSON, the 4 KB body limit, exact keys, control characters, and field limits. It uses the same email rule as the page. A filled honeypot returns `200` without storing or sending. After the visitor's hourly attempt limit and the calendar check, the insert atomically enforces the visitor, email, global, and local-day booking caps and the buffer. A rate limit returns `429` with `Retry-After`. Slot conflicts return `409`. After a successful insert, the handler writes a Google Calendar event when configured and sends confirmation with a cancel link.\n- **`functions/api/book/cancel.js` (`POST`)** checks the token in constant time, returns `404` for an unknown ID, wrong token, or past booking, and returns `200` for a valid repeat cancellation. The request that changes the row deletes any Google event and sends cancellation email.\n- **`functions/api/book/feed.js` (`GET`)** returns `404` when the token is unset, `401` on a mismatch, and `503` when the token matches and booking is off. When available, it returns bookings from seven days back through the horizon, with `Cache-Control: no-store` and UTC timestamps to the second.\n- **`scripts/book-dev.mjs`**: zero-dependency local preview server on `127.0.0.1` (`--port`, default `8801`) serving `dist/` and routing `/api/book/*` to the handlers with an in-memory `node:sqlite` D1 wrapper (`BOOK_MODE=fake` by default). The server uses its fixed loopback origin. When fake mode runs without a Resend key, it simulates delivery and prints the cancel link to stdout.\n- **`package.json`**: added `tests/book-*.test.mjs` to `test:functions`.\n- **`docs/maintaining.md`**: added the `Booking` section documenting routes, settings, secrets, defaults, and the `BOOK_MODE` switch.\n- **`tests/book-api.test.mjs`**: API contract, concurrency, cancellation, feed, upstream failure, timeout, and privacy coverage. The 20 ms SQLite-backed D1 tests exercise each booking cap and the adjacent-slot buffer, and verify confirmation delivery follows a successful insert.\n\n## Verification at `ea81931`\n\n- `npm ci`, `npm run build`, and `npm run check` passed.\n- `npm test` passed 54 of 55 tests on the first run. The remaining spec-video browser test failed a focus assertion and passed on a targeted retry.\n- `npm run test:functions` passed all 196 tests, including all booking tests.\n- The repository comment check passed against `origin/book`.\n- Local fake-mode smoke test served the booking page and slots, rejected a mismatched Host and Origin, and completed booking and cancellation using the link printed to stdout. The feed returned the cancelled booking with a whole-second `created` timestamp.\n\nBuilt with [Cloudroom](https://cloudroom.dev)\n","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openwizdev/WizSite/issues/183/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openwizdev/WizSite/issues/183/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null}},"event":"cross-referenced"}]